detaileddescription.para:
SWIM implementation is split into 3 parts: protocol logic, transport level, protocol structure. - protocol logic consists of how to react on various events, failure detection pings/acks, how often to send messages, handles the logic of the three components (failure detection, anti-entropy, dissemination);
- transport level handles routing, transport headers, packet forwarding;
- protocol structure describes how packet looks in MessagePack, how sections and headers follow each other.
